-    "Owner ruling (tvofi, 2026-10-22): \"Add checks that these seats are alive in the sweep. All these seat definitions are to be included as in the brief for the group that already includes new seat definitions, so they get permanent and wired into the repo\". This group already lands the architect/planner contracts and proposal-triage. Land, beside them, the four STANDING seats that session s4 runs, each as a role contract under dev/governance/roles/, and wire each one in.(1) Contracts. Each states purpose, model and effort, inputs (the queue lines the orchestrator sends), the instruments it drives, what it never does, report lines and footer, and its restart rule.- tick (haiku): reads orchestrator_tick.py's board and reports only owed or new items. It applies the standing filters, and the ancestor-recarry test before any REVIEW OWED. It runs in windows of about 70 min.- merge (sonnet): runs train.sh/merge_train.py with --overlap --bot-prs --approval-carry --skip-bad --free-holders, and merge_pr.sh for direct heads. It never chooses what merges, and it puts critical-path PRs first (the owner ruling carried above). After each merge it runs state_docs.py --push, and reports \"set-stage owed\".- dispatch/relay/verdict (haiku): checks the delivery row, then runs approve_held_runs, bus.sh dispatch, cloud_dispatch.py reviewer render, and the dispatch/reviewer-rev-<pr> publish. It reports fire-owed, because a subagent cannot call RemoteTrigger and the orchestrator fires. It also runs the relay loop (cloud_relay.sh --confirm), and bus.sh confirm on a merge verdict at the live head. It reports handoff-body returns.- roster (sonnet): roster_edit.py ops only. It uses --lint-cwd at a fresh origin/main. When main has moved and brief line pins drift, it merges origin/main into the roster branch; it never pushes past the lint gate. It opens the roster-batch PRs.Today these live out of the tree in the orchestrator's out-of-tree briefs directory as merge-seat.md, dispatch-relay-seat.md, overrides-s4b.md, and tick-brief-w22.txt with the briefs/tick-watcher.md it extends. Fold their substance in; keep no host paths (no-host-paths rule).(2) Wiring.- tools/audit/seat/sweep_template.md gains a step after (1) Seats: \"Standing-seat liveness\". It lists the four seats from the tracked contracts. A seat that is absent, or that finished with work still owed, is restarted in the same sweep on its contract, and the restart is logged. Its slots, if any, are declared in sweep_render.py's table.- orchestrator.md section 5 names the four standing seats and routes their work to them, never inline, paid by moving text (file at cap).- CLAUDE.md's role-contract table gains one row per contract. INSTRUMENTS.md links them.(3) Liveness check. Prefer extending pulse.py, which already reports STOPPED consumers (opener, verdict router or train, state beat), over a new check. A standing seat whose owed input has waited past its cadence prints STOPPED with the seat name. Fixture controls: an idle seat with nothing owed is not STOPPED, and one with owed input older than its cadence is.These are policy files, so the PR is approved at merge (owner, or the mandate in force with scope all). Policy caps are paid by moving text."
